# =============================================================================
# ~/.hermes/.gitignore  —  ALLOWLIST model
# =============================================================================
# This directory is a LIVE DATA directory, not just config. It holds:
#   * API keys            .env, auth.json (OAuth credential pool)
#   * personal content    sessions/, logs/, memories/, pairing/
#   * machine state       state.db, kanban.db, cache/, runtime/, sandboxes/
#   * installed bundles   scripts/whatsapp-bridge/, skills/ (image-synced)
#
# So the default here is "ignore EVERYTHING", and the handful of files worth
# versioning are re-included explicitly below. A denylist would leak the first
# time Hermes invents a new state file; this fails closed instead.
#
# To version something new: add a `!/<name>` line, then run `git status` and
# read the output before committing. Never `git add -A` blind in here.
# =============================================================================
/*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces: refuse these even if the allowlist below is loosened.
# Listed BEFORE the re-includes on purpose — in .gitignore the LAST matching
# pattern wins, so `!/.env.example` must come after `.env.*` to survive.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
auth.json
install_id
*.lock
*.pid
*.sock
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.bak-*
*.orig
models_dev_cache.json
.skills_prompt_snapshot.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALLOWLIST — the only things that get committed.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/SOUL.md
!/config.yaml
!/.env.example
!/tools/

# Hand-authored skills only. `skills/` as a whole is image-synced (bundled +
# hub-installed bundles that `hermes update` owns), so re-including it would
# commit stock files we do not maintain and churn on every upgrade. Scope the
# re-include to the category we wrote by hand; add another line per category
# if we ever author a second one.
#
# `skills/` itself is excluded by `/*` above, and git never descends into an
# excluded directory — so the child re-include alone can never win. Re-open the
# parent as a directory only (no contents), then exclude siblings again so the
# pattern stays a whitelist rather than an accident waiting for the next
# hand-authored category to appear.
!/skills/
/skills/*
!/skills/memory/
